                    <pb facs="0106" n="96" xml:id="pg96"/>
                    <p>Tonnage includes 1,600 gross tons and over, except tankers, sailers, military
                        use, and repairing. All figures in deadweight tons. Coastwise shipping of
                        United States excluded.</p>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Note.</hi>—It appears from this table that of the
                        total tonnage of United Kingdom (13,012,000), 25 per cent. (3,300,000) is
                        required for her own food used and 20 per cent. (2,660,000) is contributed
                        to Allied uses and relief. Of the total tonnage of United States
                        (4,281,000), 29 per cent. (1,250,000) is required for food uses and 28½ per
                        cent. (1,228,000) is contributed to Allied uses and relief. Of the tonnage
                        remaining, after providing for domestic food import requirements, United
                        Kingdom contributed to Allied and relief uses 27½ per cent. (2,660,000 out
                        of 9,712,000), and United States 40½ per cent. (1,228,000 out of
                        3,031,000).</p>
